k115 changed canlin.view.submission() to hand the module the submission's own JSON bytes instead of a Lua table. The built-in assistant module in src/app/assistant.c was not changed (it is the platform lane's file): it still does turn('action=' .. tostring(sub.action) .. ' values=' .. jval(sub.values, 1)). Indexing a string in Lua yields nil without an error, so the module now sends action=nil values=null - silently wrong, not loud. The change: delete the whole jstr/jval block (src/app/assistant.c:49-88) and replace the turn() call at :224 with turn(sub), so the submission's own JSON goes to the provider byte for byte. The tool-round bound is untouched by this: turn() still resets rounds = 0 and MAX_ROUNDS is still canlin.session.rounds_max (CANLIN_LLM_TOOL_ROUNDS_MAX). Depends on k115 (the assistant side), which is ready but not committed because this half was missing.

